    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 83.29. Facing a favorable matchup against Melton, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and an ideal spot in the two-hole, making him our primary engine for Runs and RBI. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** remains a high-floor, high-ceiling play at 70.33; despite a slightly tougher individual matchup against Sproat, his plate discipline and lineup security in the cleanup spot make him an auto-start. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.94) rounds out our elite tier, utilizing a strong xwOBA of .378 and an advantageous third-spot order placement to provide the consistency we need to compete in the middle of our 5x5 categories.\n\nIn terms of leverage, **Jackson Merrill** (61.40) and **Andy Pages** (58.91) represent our most intriguing starts. **Jackson Merrill** benefits significantly from a 13% platoon edge against Medina, while **Andy Pages** is tasked with maintaining our SB efficiency against Sproat. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who at 57.85 narrowly edged out our other reserves. While his 11% SP skill boost and switch-hitting versatility helped him secure a UTIL spot, he is currently a marginal play; we are prioritizing his projected stolen base upside over the current bench options like **Jorge Polanco** or **Heliot Ramos**, who did not crack the efficiency threshold today. \n\nWe are monitoring the health of our depth, as **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** remain sidelined on the IL, severely limiting our ability to rotate for late-breaking weather or lineup changes. **Liam Hicks** (53.47) is a viable start at C1 due to his dynamic platoon advantage (11%) and leadoff duties, but he remains a volatile piece. With **Brayan Rocchio** (47.05) relegated to the bottom of the order and struggling with a negative adjustment for his #9 spot, we will be watching his early at-bats closely to see if he can provide any speed-based value before we look to pinch-hit with options like **Coby Mayo** or **Josh Jung** if they receive late-game usage.",
